From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:52:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): wire mHC async Sinkhorn split across
 model and DSpark


Wire mHC async Sinkhorn finalize split (mhc.async_sinkhorn) across the
DeepSeek-V4.1 target model and DSpark speculator so critical-path RMSNorm
completes immediately while Sinkhorn projection runs on aux_stream().

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Move Sinkhorn projection off the decode critical path (-1.00% tp3
           engine grid, c1 tpot_p50 -0.34 ms / -2.35% across 2 live boots).
Quality: Bit-exact (128/128 greedy outputs_sha256 match, KL=0, ppl +0.000%).
Tests: pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py (15 passed)
       + 2-boot live tp3-triangle screen (PR #1264).
Upstream-status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang runtime optimization.
